    "background_story": "Cowboy was a rugged individualist who roamed the open ranges of the American West. His name was a testament to his profession, but also reflected his substantial and unyielding character. With a strong jawline and piercing blue eyes, Cowboy was a man of few words, but his presence was always felt. He lived by a code of honor and integrity, never backing down from a challenge or abandoning those in need. Cowboy's substantival nature was rooted in his unwavering commitment to his values and principles. He was a rock, unshakeable and unbreakable, and those who knew him respected him for it. Whether facing a raging storm or a rival rancher, Cowboy stood firm, a substantial force to be reckoned with.",
